  "prefLabel": "Nur 501.03 Professional Duties",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nur 501.03 Professional Duties.\n\n(a) An Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) shall, pursuant to RSA 326-B:11, III. and RSA 326-B:37, II.(h) be under a professional duty to comply with the requirements of the controlled drug prescription health and safety program (PDMP), RSA 318-B:31-38, and all administrative rules of the board of pharmacy adopted thereunder.\n\n(b) Pursuant to RSA 318-B:36, the following actions shall result in a disciplinary proceeding and the imposition of sanctions upon an APRN by the board in accordance with its rules:\n\n(1) Prescribing or dispensing of controlled substances in schedule II-IV without having registered with the PDMP;\n\n(2) The knowing disclosure of PDMP information by a person authorized to receive it, in a manner that violates RSA 318-B or administrative rules of the board of pharmacy;\n\n(3) The use of information from the PDMP by a person authorized to receive it, for a purpose that violates RSA 318-B or administrative rules of the board of pharmacy; or\n\n(4) Permitting the use or disclosure of information from the PDMP under control of the nurse by a person not authorized to receive it, in violation of RSA 381-B or administrative rules of the board of pharmacy.\n\nSource. #7769, eff 10-1-02; ss by #8873, eff 4-24-07; ss by #10300, eff 3-22-13; ss by #13673, eff 6-23-23; ss by #14297, eff 8-25-25, EXPIRES: 8-25-35 (formerly Nur 501.04)",
